{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012LjGdddphqzpdKK8aCKH3P","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t14/shadow/exec-ws/first-derivation.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fd0a6bd-2533-418b-b997-b2ae4d208f3a","uuid":"c4c123da-6a32-427f-8279-5d6d2ab63d8c","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:43:52.984Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t14/shadow/exec-ws/first-derivation.md","content":"# First derivation (E-A) — digit-string tie inspection\n\nMethod (no floating point anywhere): each input is kept as its exact decimal\ndigit string. Steps per item:\n\n1. Record the sign; drop it from the digit string.\n2. Split at `.` into integer digits and fraction digits (empty fraction if no\n   point).\n3. If the fraction has ≤ 2 digits, no rounding occurs; pad with zeros to\n   exactly 2.\n4. Otherwise classify the tail beyond the second fractional digit:\n   - **below half** — third fractional digit < 5: truncate to 2 digits;\n   - **above half** — third fractional digit > 5, or = 5 with any nonzero\n     digit after it: increment the 2-digit fraction;\n   - **exact tie** — third fractional digit = 5 and every later digit is 0 (or\n     absent): keep the 2-digit fraction if its last (hundredths) digit is\n     even, otherwise increment it.\n5. Increments carry through the digit string right-to-left (99 → 00 with +1\n   into the integer part; 999999 + 1 → 1000000).\n6. Comma-group the integer part every three digits from the right.\n7. Prepend nothing for positives; wrap the unsigned result in parentheses for\n   negatives. (Half-even is symmetric, so rounding the unsigned magnitude\n   equals rounding the signed value; sign ordering cannot change the digits.)\n\n## Per-item work\n\n| input | sign | frac tail class | hundredths digit | rounded magnitude | formatted |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `2.675` | + | tie (`5`) | 7 odd → increment | 2.68 | `2.68` |\n| `-1234.5` | − | no rounding (1 digit) | pad | 1234.50 | `(1,234.50)` |\n| `0.005` | + | tie (`5`) | 0 even → keep | 0.00 | `0.00` |\n| `1000` | + | no fraction | pad | 1000.00 | `1,000.00` |\n| `-0.125` | − | tie (`5`) | 2 even → keep | 0.12 | `(0.12)` |\n| `999999.995` | + | tie (`5`) | 9 odd → increment, carry 999999.99→1000000.00 | 1000000.00 | `1,000,000.00` |\n| `0.045` | + | tie (`5`) | 4 even → keep | 0.04 | `0.04` |\n| `12345.675` | + | tie (`5`) | 7 odd → increment | 12345.68 | `12,345.68` |\n| `-2.5` | − | no rounding (1 digit) | pad | 2.50 | `(2.50)` |\n| `0` | + | no fraction | pad | 0.00 | `0.00` |\n| `7.375` | + | tie (`5`) | 7 odd → increment | 7.38 | `7.38` |\n| `-999.985` | − | tie (`5`) | 8 even → keep | 999.98 | `(999.98)` |\n\nNotes on the adversarial traps, handled by construction:\n\n- `2.675`, `12345.675`, `7.375`, `0.045`, `-0.125`, `-999.985`, `0.005`,\n  `999999.995` are exact ties in decimal; a binary-float parse would silently\n  turn several of them (e.g. 2.675 → 2.67499…) into below-half cases. The\n  digit-string method never leaves decimal digits, so ties stay ties.\n- Half-up would give 0.01, 0.05, (0.13), (999.99) on the even-keep items;\n  half-even keeps 0.00, 0.04, (0.12), (999.98).\n- `999999.995` requires full carry propagation into a new leading digit and a\n  new comma group: `1,000,000.00`.\n- Negative ties round identically on the magnitude because ties-to-even is\n  symmetric about zero; parentheses are applied after rounding.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
